cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  BSARD Retrieval (RQ2): Naive, Metadata-Aware and
  PageIndex Retrieval Arms over Belgian Statutory Law
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using these
  metadata. Please also cite the underlying BSARD dataset
  (see DATA_LICENSE.md).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Marios
    family-names: Paschalidis
    email: paschalidismarios@gmail.com
    affiliation: KU Leuven
repository-code: "https://github.com/MariusPasch/bsard-rag-thesis"
abstract: >-
  Code and experiments for RQ2 of a master's thesis at
  KU Leuven: a per-document comparison of three retrieval
  arms over Belgian statutory law — Arm 1 (naive
  chunk-and-embed), Arm 2A (metadata-aware structural
  retrieval), and Arm 2B (PageIndex LLM tree navigation),
  plus an agentic Arm 2C corrective-loop extension — all
  grounded in the Belgian Statutory Article Retrieval
  Dataset (BSARD).
keywords:
  - information retrieval
  - legal NLP
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - BSARD
  - structural retrieval
  - PageIndex
license: MIT
